# =============================================================
# SUPABASE SETUP GUIDE FOR TEAMMATES
# =============================================================
#
# STEP 1 — Create your .env file
#   Create a new file called exactly:  .env
#   It must be placed in the "thryft" folder (same folder as pubspec.yaml).
#   This is the correct location:
#
#     Group-Project/
#     └── thryft/          <-- your .env goes HERE
#         ├── pubspec.yaml
#         ├── .env         <-- correct location
#         ├── lib/
#         └── ...
#
#   DO NOT put it inside lib/, assets/, or anywhere else.
#
# STEP 2 — Get your Supabase credentials
#   1. Go to https://supabase.com and sign in (or create an account)
#   2. Ask George to add you to the project, OR open the shared project
#   3. In the Supabase dashboard, go to:
#        Project Settings (gear icon, bottom left) → API
#   4. You will see two values you need:
#        - "Project URL"     → copy this for SUPABASE_URL below
#        - "anon / public"   → copy this for SUPABASE_ANON_KEY below
#
# STEP 3 — Paste your values into your .env file
#   Copy the two lines below into your .env file and replace the
#   placeholder text with your real values (no quotes needed).
#
# STEP 4 — Run flutter pub get
#   In your terminal, from inside the thryft/ folder, run:
#        flutter pub get
#   Then hot restart the app (not just hot reload).
#
# STEP 5 — Verify it works
#   The app should launch without any "null check" or "env not loaded" errors.
#   If you see errors, double-check the .env file is in the right place.
#
# =============================================================
# YOUR .env FILE SHOULD CONTAIN EXACTLY THESE TWO LINES:
# =============================================================

SUPABASE_URL=your_supabase_project_url_here
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your_supabase_anon_key_here
